## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzle
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1913-12-21
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with an empty cross-shaped centre (shown as _); the three squares of the second row are printed with the letters F, U, N. No credit, no number. The clue list has 30 clues: none is printed for 2-3 (SALES), and three pairs are misprinted (38-39 for 18-19, 10-12 for 10-18, 26-30 for 23-30), kept as printed. Instructions as printed: "Fill in the small squares with words which agree with the following definitions:". Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1913_12_21_68.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1913_12_28_78.png (printed upside down), by Claude, 2026-11-16.


